  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, poll fixed for 15 January 1931; the six retiring members were returned unopposed (Northern Whig, 1 January 1931, p. 6; Belfast Telegraph, 6 January 1931, p. 6). The retiring members were named in the nomination-week notice (Northern Whig, 1 January 1931): 'All were returned unopposed three years ago with the exception of Mr. Atkinson, school teacher, who was co-opted.' The Belfast Telegraph's nomination-day survey states that, except for Bangor and Portrush, no urban election in Ulster was contested, so these six held their seats without a poll. Returned unopposed."
